    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 45 tests pass. \n\nThe change adds `checkDigit` \u2014 a single Luhn check digit over the digits of `customerCode` \u2014 to the owner response:\n\n1. **`util/CheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 a `luhn(String)` helper that runs the standard Luhn algorithm over the digit characters of a string, ignoring the `-` separators in the customer code.\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the read-only `checkDigit` field (integer 0\u20139) on the owner schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the property.\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired a MapStruct expression mapping `checkDigit` to `CheckDigit.luhn(owner.getCustomerCode())`, matching how the other derived fields (e.g. `membershipNumber`, `identityKey`) are computed at mapping time.\n\nThe Cp31 test \u2014 which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact digit \u2014 passes, and the full suite is green (45/45).",
